.TH OFM 1 "2026-11-27" "ofm 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ofm \- keyboard-first two-panel file manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ofm
.RI [ LEFT_DIR " [" RIGHT_DIR ]]
.br
.B ofm
.BR \-h | \-\-help
.br
.B ofm
.BR \-V | \-\-version
.br
.B ofm \-\-dump\-keys
.I PRESET
.SH DESCRIPTION
OFM (Orthodox File Manager) is a two\-panel GTK 4 file manager with a command line,
an embedded terminal, background file operations, a viewer, file search and
read\-only archive browsing.
.PP
Without arguments the panels of the previous session are restored.
When a directory is given, the stored panel paths are not restored:
.I LEFT_DIR
is shown on the left and
.I RIGHT_DIR
(default: the home directory) on the right.
.PP
Only one instance runs per login session.
Starting
.B ofm
again presents the existing window.
Given directories open there:
.I LEFT_DIR
in the active panel and
.I RIGHT_DIR
in the other one, relative to the directory of the new command.
A locked tab is left as it is; the directory opens in a new tab.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-dump\-keys " PRESET"
Print the key reference of a built\-in keymap preset
.RB ( far ", " tc " or " mc )
as Markdown and exit.
Your own
.I keymap.toml
is not applied.
.PP
These three options need no display.
.SH KEYS
The default preset follows Far Manager.
Press
.B F1
in the program for all keys.
.TP
.B Tab
Switch the active panel.
.TP
.BR F3 ", " F4
View, edit.
.TP
.BR F5 ", " F6 ", " F7 ", " F8
Copy, move, make directory, delete (to Trash).
.TP
.BR F9 ", " F10
Menu bar, quit.
.TP
.B Ctrl+O
Show or hide the panels (full terminal).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ofm/config.toml
Settings.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ofm/keymap.toml
Key bindings on top of the preset.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ofm/menu.toml
User menu.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ofm/themes/
User themes.
.TP
.I .ofm\-menu.toml
Per\-directory user menu, used only after you trust it.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/ofm/
Session and history.
.PP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME
defaults to
.IR ~/.config ,
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME
to
.IR ~/.local/state .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR VISUAL ", " EDITOR
Editor for F4 when none is configured.
.TP
.B SHELL
Shell of the command line and terminal when none is configured.
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Log filter, for example
.IR ofm=debug .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 2 on a wrong command line.
.SH SEE ALSO
The user guide in
.IR /usr/share/doc/ofm/USER\-GUIDE.md .
.SH BUGS
https://github.com/ms\-coder/orthodox/issues
